\f0\fs24 \cf2 Look at the Dome Gallery and compare the historical photograph with the current display. The atmosphere remains the same, although the arches once were decorated with vegetal frescoes, which are no longer there. But the objects you see today, such as the majolica on the table or the overdoors by Andrea Lilio, are a testament to the refinement that has always distinguished this house. And what about the large canvas by Giovan Pietro Gnocchi? It\'92s now in the dining room. And the polyptych above the table with the majolica? Have you already seen this work... where?\
